  "hindi": "एक स्त्री के पुत्रों में ज्येष्ठ का भाग — ब्राह्मणों के लिए बकरे, क्षत्रियों के लिए घोड़े, वैश्यों के लिए गायें, शूद्रों के लिए भेड़ें।",
  "english": "Among sons of one wife, the eldest's share [is]: goats for brahmins, horses for kshatriyas, cows for vaishyas, sheep for shudras.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The stand-alone '-' is the edition's join mark (a pause), not a word. The predicate is omitted in Sanskrit. 'ajāḥ' and 'avayaḥ' are plural forms that can be masculine or feminine, so goats and sheep in general. 'Of one wife' is the literal sense of eka-strī; sons of a single wife as opposed to the several wives of unit 13.",
