  "notes": "'parivāpa' is kept untranslated (sense uncertain; household effects is a guess). 'kṛṣṇam' is a bare neuter 'black [thing]'; it may be a separate item (black things) or may qualify what follows (black grain / black iron); not settled. 'dhānya-āyasam' is read as a dvandva 'grain [and] iron-ware'. 'go-śakaṭa' = cart for cattle (ox-cart). 'bhukta' = used, enjoyed. 'gṛha-parivāpa' is taken as one item, 'house-parivāpa'.",
